<title>UK: Aluminium output rose in August - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output rose in August - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in August rose to 50,800 tonnes compared with 50,600 in July and 47,700 in August 1995, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in August (31 days) was 1.574 million tonnes, compared with 1.569 million in July (31 days) and 1.480 million in August 1995.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>				Aug'96   Jul'96   Aug'95</p>
<p>    Africa		    92	 91	 53</p>
<p>    North America	  496	494	476</p>
<p>    Latin America	  178	179	177</p>
<p>    Asia		     135	134	140</p>
<p>    Europe West	    269	271	n/a</p>
<p>    Europe East/Central  262	260	n/a</p>
<p>    Oceania		  142	140	134</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
